I haven't added the metadata fetch. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0`, and a change to that grant has to be made in the graph declaration, not in the node body. I've left a note in the source. The notifier-only version is below. If the grant is extended, the `http-client` import and the fetch can be added then. Interpolating raw input text into a URL on an internal host also needs URL-encoding and a review of what that host can reach.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{digest, published-digest};

    import aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0;

    export run: func(composed: digest) -> published-digest;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::notifier;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(composed: Digest) -> PublishedDigest {
        // NOTE: The per-call enrichment fetch from metadata.internal.example is
        // intentionally not implemented here. This node's `with` clause grants only
        // aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0. Adding an http-client import requires the grant to
        // be extended in the graph declaration first.

        let kept = composed.entries.iter().filter(|e| e.kept).count();
        let message = format!(
            "digest {}: {} kept of {} considered. {}",
            composed.date,
            kept,
            composed.considered.len(),
            composed.overview
        );

        let published = notifier::notify(&message);

        PublishedDigest {
            date: composed.date,
            considered: composed.considered,
            published,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

